WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:05.146
At daybreak I woke up to a series of awful screams from Bill.

2
00:00:05.148 --> 00:00:11.399
They weren't yells, howls, shouts, whoops, or yelps, like you'd expect from a man's vocal cords.

3
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:19.374
Instead they were simply shameless, terrifying, humiliating screams, like when women see a ghost or a caterpillar.

4
00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:26.486
It's an awful thing to hear a strong, desperate, fat man shrieking uncontrollably in a cave at daybreak.

5
00:00:26.487 --> 00:00:31.353
I jumped up to see what was wrong and saw Red Chief sitting on Bill's chest.

6
00:00:31.354 --> 00:00:38.274
One of the boy's hands held a hank of Bill's hair while the other hand waved the sharp knife we'd used for slicing bacon.

7
00:00:38.275 --> 00:00:42.098
Red Chief was about to give Bill a very bad haircut.

8
00:00:42.099 --> 00:00:44.993
I pried the knife out of the kid's fingers.

9
00:00:44.994 --> 00:00:50.381
"Stop it! Leave Bill alone! Lie down and stay down!" I yelled.

10
00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:53.658
But from that moment, Bill's spirit was broken.

11
00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:59.970
He lay down on his side of the bed, and never closed an eye again in sleep as long as that boy was with us.

12
00:00:59.971 --> 00:01:07.494
I dozed off for a while, but I remembered later that Red Chief had said I was to be burned at the stake at the rising of the sun.

13
00:01:07.495 --> 00:01:13.614
I wasn't nervous or afraid, but I sat up, lit my pipe, and leaned against a rock.

14
00:01:13.615 --> 00:01:16.916
"Why are you getting up so soon, Sam?" asked Bill.

15
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:23.609
"Me?" I said. "Oh, I got a little pain in my shoulder. I thought sitting up would make it feel better."

16
00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:29.310
"You're a liar!" said Bill. "You're supposed to be burned at sunrise, and you're afraid he'll do it.

17
00:01:29.311 --> 00:01:32.048
And he would too, if he could find a match.

18
00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:38.542
This is awful, Sam. Do you think anyone will pay good money to get a rotten kid like that back?"

19
00:01:38.543 --> 00:01:43.629
"Sure," I said. "A wild kid like that is just the kind that parents spoil.

20
00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:50.113
Now you and the chief get up and cook breakfast. I'll go up on top of this mountain and see if anything is happening."

21
00:01:50.114 --> 00:01:54.375
I hiked over to the peak of the little mountain and looked toward the horizon.

22
00:01:54.376 --> 00:02:04.199
When I spied the town of Summit, I expected to see packs of villagers armed with axes and pitchforks running around the countryside searching for the dastardly kidnappers.

23
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:10.301
But what I saw was a peaceful landscape and one man plowing a field with a grayish-brown mule.

24
00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:18.468
Nobody was searching the creek for a drowned child. No messengers ran here and there bringing news of no news to the worried parents.

25
00:02:18.469 --> 00:02:25.179
Everything I could see from the top of that mountain looked calm and drowsy, if not already asleep.

26
00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:31.958
"Perhaps they haven't yet discovered that the wolves have stolen away their tender little lamb," I said to myself.

27
00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:34.704
Then I swallowed and thought of Red Chief.

28
00:02:34.705 --> 00:02:40.847
"Heaven help the wolves!" I yelled to the serene valley and went down the mountain to breakfast.

29
00:02:40.848 --> 00:02:46.441
When I got back to the hideout, I found Bill with his back up against the wall of the cave.

30
00:02:46.442 --> 00:02:52.899
He was breathing hard. The boy was holding a coconut-sized rock in both hands and was shaking it at him.

31
00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.207
"I'll smash you with this!" Red Chief shouted.

32
00:02:56.208 --> 00:03:03.267
Bill saw me and started talking fast. "He dropped a red-hot boiled potato down my back.

33
00:03:03.268 --> 00:03:10.169
Then he mashed it with his foot! It hurt so much, I slapped him. Have you got your gun, Sam?"

34
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:15.792
I grabbed the rock away from the boy. "Come on, now, you two," I said. "Play nice."

35
00:03:15.793 --> 00:03:23.459
"I'll fix you," the kid told Bill. "No man ever struck Red Chief and got away with it. You'll be sorry!"

36
00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:28.650
After breakfast, the kid took a piece of leather with strings wrapped around it out of his pocket.

37
00:03:28.651 --> 00:03:31.839
He went outside the cave and started to unwind it.

38
00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:38.464
"What's he up to now?" asked Bill in a scared voice. "You don't think he'll run away, do you, Sam?"

39
00:03:38.465 --> 00:03:43.766
When he asked me this, Bill sounded hopeful as he pressed his hands together in a kind of prayer.

40
00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:50.631
"Nope," I said. "He's not much of a homebody. We've got to think up some plan about the ransom.

41
00:03:50.632 --> 00:03:57.400
There's no excitement around Summit about the boy's disappearance, but maybe they haven't realized that he's gone yet.

42
00:03:57.401 --> 00:04:03.886
His folks may think he's spending the night with an aunt or one of his neighbors. Anyhow he'll be missed today.

43
00:04:03.887 --> 00:04:09.753
Tonight we've got to get a message to his father demanding the two thousand dollars for his return."

44
00:04:09.754 --> 00:04:16.988
Just then we heard a different kind of war whoop, like David might have shouted when he knocked out Goliath in ancient times.

45
00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:20.218
"OOOUUU-WOWWW!"

46
00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:23.090
"He's got a sling!" I yelled. "Look out!"

47
00:04:23.091 --> 00:04:29.409
Red Chief started whirling the weapon around his head, and I ducked in time, but Bill didn't.

48
00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:34.869
Then I heard a heavy thud, and Bill screamed like he'd been shot through the head with an arrow.

49
00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:40.884
A smooth black rock the size of an egg had caught Bill just behind his left ear.

50
00:04:40.885 --> 00:04:48.699
He wobbled, lost his balance, and then fell across the pan of hot water on the fire that had been used for washing the dishes.

51
00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.300
I dragged him out and poured cool water on his head for half an hour.

52
00:04:53.301 --> 00:05:02.432
Finally Bill sat up and felt behind his ear. He asked, "Sam, did you ever learn the Ten Commandments when you were a kid?"

53
00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:04.941
"Yeah, sure," I said.

54
00:05:04.942 --> 00:05:07.806
"Do you remember the sixth one?" he asked.

55
00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:11.233
I took a wild guess. "Do not kill?"

56
00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:14.214
"I thought of an exception," Bill said.

57
00:05:14.215 --> 00:05:16.651
"You'll feel better soon," I said.

58
00:05:16.652 --> 00:05:21.645
Bill grabbed my hand. "You won't go away and leave me here alone, will you, Sam?"

59
00:05:21.646 --> 00:05:26.992
I went out and caught that boy and shook him until his freckles rattled.

